  "verbalization": "Dorsmanin D appears to have a shared target of Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like across multiple paths, suggesting a common mechanism of action. This enzyme is targeted by several compounds, including 23-Hydroxy-3-Oxoolean-12-En-27-Oic Acid, 5-Hydroxy-2-Methylchromone-7-O-Rutinoside, and Picrinine, all of which are implicated in targeting the replicase polyprotein 1ab. The integration of these pathways implies that Dorsmanin D may act through a common downstream mechanism, possibly by modulating the activity of Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, which in turn influences the replicase polyprotein 1ab. The evidence suggests a potential role for Dorsmanin D in regulating the replicase polyprotein 1ab through a pathway involving Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
